                        "form": "дуэ́тах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6590c024-c21b-309f-8978-c6443c29bf48",
                        "entry_id": "3d873571-960e-35aa-9860-9606728f9160",
                        "glosses": [
                            "в спорте, музыке, танцах и т. п. — команда или ансамбль из двух исполнителей, выступающих вместе, также творческий союз двух исполнителей"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "55be6b1e-718b-4300-a661-7fe7d7a1fd16",
                                "sense_id": "6590c024-c21b-309f-8978-c6443c29bf48",
                                "text": "Геннадий Маковский и Генрих Ротман, по-моему, лучший клоунский дуэт во все времена."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e5427972-6365-4072-b46e-6504e08acfcc",
                                "sense_id": "6590c024-c21b-309f-8978-c6443c29bf48",
                                "text": "Появилась надежда, что в театре возродится традиция звездных дуэтов, выступления которых некогда обсуждала вся Москва."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9bffa778-7618-38b0-ad96-c564b13fde3e",
                        "entry_id": "3d873571-960e-35aa-9860-9606728f9160",
                        "glosses": [
                            "инструментальное или вокальное музыкальное произведение для исполнения вдвоём"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8dbadc2d-1a79-41be-81de-9126a2a3b289",
                                "sense_id": "9bffa778-7618-38b0-ad96-c564b13fde3e",
                                "text": "Особенно нам нравилось петь дуэт Лизы и Полины из «Пиковой дамы» Чайковского — конечно, по слуху, не по нотам."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d67f1309-391f-39e6-bcc2-173c70bff202",
                        "entry_id": "3d873571-960e-35aa-9860-9606728f9160",
                        "glosses": [
                            "редк. название полифонической пьесы с двумя равнозначными партиями-голосами"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e71a6c87-c611-4fdc-b4e8-b618765ae886",
                                "sense_id": "d67f1309-391f-39e6-bcc2-173c70bff202",
                                "text": "4 дуэт в «Упражнении для клавира» И. С. Баха."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ee6e5526-043e-46d5-b877-18cafe9b802b",
                        "source_entry_id": "3d873571-960e-35aa-9860-9606728f9160",
                        "source_sense_description": "ансамбль, команда из двух исполнителей",
                        "target_lang_word": "duet",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "duet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "892c16da-4270-31db-acf4-1102adfebae5",
                                        "entry_id": "1614c731-5de6-30b0-96de-56ee18876627",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A musical composition in two parts, each performed by a single voice (singer, instrument or univoce ensemble)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c1493c97-897e-3530-b363-6460ed3c7c68",
                                        "entry_id": "1614c731-5de6-30b0-96de-56ee18876627",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A song composed for and/or performed by a duo."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "44e630bc-dd48-3617-9ba8-8c5939d7701d",
                                        "entry_id": "1614c731-5de6-30b0-96de-56ee18876627",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A pair or couple, especially one that is harmonious or elegant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b153722b-e4a3-418e-840d-91d3856f9724",
                                                "sense_id": "44e630bc-dd48-3617-9ba8-8c5939d7701d",
                                                "text": "The fare is Caribbean with an Asian touch — millefeuille of sun-dried tomato, Paris mushrooms and chargrilled local asparagus followed by a duet of chicken and shrimp..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "duet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "12fe1a2d-c5e8-34aa-8eb6-e0e4c5401f68",
                                        "entry_id": "1562419b-15be-37b8-8e70-687bc0ebd1e4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To perform a duet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c448ab6-42e6-4a04-bccd-e9381e8395b3",
                                                "sense_id": "12fe1a2d-c5e8-34aa-8eb6-e0e4c5401f68",
                                                "text": "1822, Lord Byron, Letter to Mr. Moore, Pisa, July 12, 1822, in The Letters of George Gordon Byron, edited by Mathilde Blind, London: Walter Scott, 1887, p. 277, https://books.google.ca/books?id=-DF4Zs_eezUC&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false\nWhen you can spare time from duetting, coquetting, and claretting with your Hibernians of both sexes, let me have a line from you."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a17d041d-f35d-4de5-b729-3c881870ce88",
                                                "sense_id": "12fe1a2d-c5e8-34aa-8eb6-e0e4c5401f68",
                                                "text": "He was about as accordantly coupled with Dr. Middleton in discourse as a drum duetting with a bass-viol […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92a065c4-9718-421f-ad7b-03811d53134c",
                                                "sense_id": "12fe1a2d-c5e8-34aa-8eb6-e0e4c5401f68",
                                                "text": "‘Ti-yi-yi-yime is on my side, yes it is,’ I used to yodel, duetting with Mick Jagger as I gyrated alone in my student room."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "31eaf6a1-1daa-3ca9-a816-d179c19cd045",
                                        "entry_id": "1562419b-15be-37b8-8e70-687bc0ebd1e4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To communicate (warnings, mating calls, etc.) through song."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79a5e81e-1f4a-4f41-bc32-384c45ba2367",
                                                "sense_id": "31eaf6a1-1daa-3ca9-a816-d179c19cd045",
                                                "text": "1975, Edward O. Wilson, Sociobiology: The New Synthesis, Belknap Press, p. 223,\nDuetting species are typically monogamous."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d82c8fa-1d6a-4c7c-b4c8-7ab6c55d73b2",
                                                "sense_id": "31eaf6a1-1daa-3ca9-a816-d179c19cd045",
                                                "text": "In several dozen species of birds there has been found a phenomenon known as duetting, or antiphonal singing: the first part of a song is executed by one partner of a pair, then the other partner very promptly chimes in to sing the second part."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1cba51ee-b992-335e-a63d-d3a5bd29e903",
                                        "entry_id": "1562419b-15be-37b8-8e70-687bc0ebd1e4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To perform (sing, play, etc.) as a duet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fa50365-2eb0-4f86-8b82-554579c2ca8b",
                                                "sense_id": "1cba51ee-b992-335e-a63d-d3a5bd29e903",
                                                "text": "Peena and Queena are duetting a giggle-for-giggle […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21c6b956-9116-423b-bbdc-ad2fbcf8358d",
                                                "sense_id": "1cba51ee-b992-335e-a63d-d3a5bd29e903",
                                                "text": "After the Lord's Prayer the Missionaries duetted a hymn while the children stared at me."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5a1e0dac-feab-3aaa-bbd2-e8bc1b4b338b",
                                        "entry_id": "1562419b-15be-37b8-8e70-687bc0ebd1e4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(of two people) To say at the same time, to chorus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "761e9a5b-9012-47e7-ac7b-574b5ddded83",
                                                "sense_id": "5a1e0dac-feab-3aaa-bbd2-e8bc1b4b338b",
                                                "text": "“My dear papa!” duetted the girls; but there was something in the husband and father's face, that told the three ladies it would be worse than useless to raise that question at present."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6831adae-30c9-432a-b16c-3e5e9bfbe97a",
                                                "sense_id": "5a1e0dac-feab-3aaa-bbd2-e8bc1b4b338b",
                                                "text": "1884, Anonymous, A Speculation, Denver: D. M. Richards, Chapter 12, p. 50, https://books.google.ca/books?id=RsFQAQAAIAAJ&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false\n“A bear!” exclaimed the Major, jumping up and coming forward.\n“A bear!” dueted the Doctor and Right Rev., pressing hastily to the front."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
